    "title": "News From Around the Web",
    "text": "• A lawsuit alleges that U.S. Rep. Eric Swalwell is misrepresenting his residency in California.\n• Erika Kirk is seeking a speedy trial in the case of her husband's alleged assassin, citing undue delay.\n• Stock futures indicate potential losses following Donald Trump's threat of tariffs over Greenland.\n• The Justice Department plans to pursue charges related to a protest inside a church, criticizing Don Lemon's coverage.\n• Over 100 clergy members staged a sit-in at Target headquarters, demanding action.\n• Donald Trump shared private messages from leaders regarding Greenland and reiterated his threats to acquire the territory.\n• A multi-vehicle pileup occurred in Michigan due to a snowstorm, resulting in numerous injuries.\n• An article discusses the potential health risks associated with flame retardants in household items.\n• Economic data indicates growing strength on Main Street, with rising wages and retail sales.\n• BlackRock CEO Larry Fink will address the World Economic Forum, acknowledging a crisis of legitimacy for Davos and the economic system it represents.",
